    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15134" root="رخل" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِخْلٌ</span></b>  <i>A ewe-lamb;</i> (S, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِخْلَةٌ</span></b>  and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَخِلٌ</span></b> : (K:) the male is called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَمَلٌ</span>: (S:) pl.
[of pauc.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْخُلٌ</span> (K) and [of mult.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِخَالٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُخَالٌ</span> (S, K,) which last is of an extr. form,
(TA,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِخْلَانٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَخَلَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِخَلَةٌ</span>. (K.)

